## Step 3: Gradual Migration Strategy

### Option A: Side-by-Side Deployment (Recommended)

Deploy both versions simultaneously and gradually migrate traffic:

```javascript
// server.js
const insecureApp = require('./app');
const secureApp = require('./app.secure');

// Old app on port 3000 (to be deprecated)
insecureApp.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Legacy API on port 3000 (deprecated)');
});

// New secure app on port 3001
secureApp.listen(3001, () => {
  console.log('Secure API on port 3001');
});
```

**Traffic Migration:**
1. Week 1: Deploy secure version, test with 10% of traffic
2. Week 2: Migrate 50% of traffic if no issues
3. Week 3: Migrate 100% of traffic
4. Week 4: Deprecate old version

### Option B: Feature Flags

Enable security features gradually:

```javascript
// app.js with feature flags
require('dotenv').config();

const enableAuth = process.env.ENABLE_AUTH === 'true';
const enableRateLimit = process.env.ENABLE_RATE_LIMITING === 'true';

if (enableAuth) {
  app.get('/api/users', authenticateJWT, (req, res) => { /* ... */ });
} else {
  app.get('/users', (req, res) => { /* ... */ }); // legacy
}
```

