## 🔐 Secret Rotation Strategy

### DON'T Do This (Unsafe):
```javascript
// ❌ NEVER extract or display secret values
console.log('Current JWT_SECRET:', process.env.JWT_SECRET.substring(0, 4) + '...');
// ❌ NEVER store secrets in spreadsheets or documents
// ❌ NEVER email or message secrets
// ❌ NEVER commit secrets to git
```

### DO This Instead:

#### 1. Automated Rotation with AWS Secrets Manager
```bash
# Create rotation Lambda function
aws lambda create-function \
  --function-name RotateJWTSecret \
  --runtime nodejs18.x \
  --handler index.handler \
  --role arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/LambdaSecretsRotation

# Enable automatic rotation
aws secretsmanager rotate-secret \
  --secret-id app/production/JWT_SECRET \
  --rotation-lambda-arn arn:aws:lambda:region:account:function:RotateJWTSecret \
  --rotation-rules AutomaticallyAfterDays=30
```

#### 2. Manual Rotation Procedure (if secrets manager not available)
```javascript
// rotation-script.js
const crypto = require('crypto');

// Generate new secret (NEVER log or display this)
const newSecret = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');

// Update in secrets manager
await secretsManager.updateSecret('app/production/JWT_SECRET', newSecret);

// Wait for propagation
console.log('Waiting for secret propagation...');
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 5000));

// Verify update
console.log('✅ Secret rotated successfully');
// DO NOT log the actual value
```

#### 3. Zero-Downtime Rotation Strategy
```javascript
// Support both old and new secrets during rotation period
const authenticateJWT = (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.substring(7);

  try {
    // Try new secret first
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, appSecrets.JWT_SECRET);
    req.user = decoded;
    return next();
  } catch (error) {
    // Fallback to old secret (during rotation window only)
    if (appSecrets.JWT_SECRET_OLD) {
      try {
        const decoded = jwt.verify(token, appSecrets.JWT_SECRET_OLD);
        req.user = decoded;
        return next();
      } catch (oldError) {
        // Both failed
      }
    }
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
  }
};
```

