# Security Quick Reference Card

## 🔒 Essential Security Checklist

### Before Every Deployment
- [ ] All environment variables configured
- [ ] HTTPS/TLS enabled
- [ ] Strong secrets generated (min 32 chars)
- [ ] Authentication enabled on all sensitive endpoints
- [ ] Input validation on all user inputs
- [ ] Rate limiting configured
- [ ] Security headers enabled (Helmet)
- [ ] Error handling doesn't expose internals
- [ ] Logging/monitoring active
- [ ] Dependencies updated and audited
- [ ] Security tests passing

---

## 🚨 Common Vulnerabilities Quick Fix

### 1. No Authentication
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json(users);
});

// GOOD ✅
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  res.json(users);
});
```

### 2. SQL Injection
```javascript
// BAD ❌
const query = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${req.params.id}`;

// GOOD ✅
const query = 'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1';
const result = await pool.query(query, [req.params.id]);
```

### 3. XSS
```javascript
// BAD ❌
res.send(`<h1>Hello ${req.query.name}</h1>`);

// GOOD ✅
const xss = require('xss-clean');
app.use(xss());
res.json({ message: `Hello ${req.query.name}` });
```

### 4. Missing Security Headers
```javascript
// BAD ❌
// No security headers

// GOOD ✅
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());
```

### 5. No Rate Limiting
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.post('/login', loginHandler);

// GOOD ✅
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const limiter = rateLimit({ windowMs: 15*60*1000, max: 5 });
app.post('/login', limiter, loginHandler);
```

### 6. Weak Password Storage
```javascript
// BAD ❌
const password = req.body.password;
user.password = password; // Plain text!

// GOOD ✅
const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');
const hash = await bcrypt.hash(req.body.password, 12);
user.password = hash;
```

### 7. Information Disclosure
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  res.status(500).json({ error: err.stack });
});

// GOOD ✅
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
});
```

### 8. Missing Input Validation
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const user = getUser(req.params.id);
});

// GOOD ✅
const { param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');
app.get('/users/:id', 
  param('id').isInt({min: 1}),
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }
    const user = getUser(req.params.id);
  }
);
```

### 9. Insecure CORS
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.use(cors()); // Allows all origins!

// GOOD ✅
app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://yourdomain.com'],
  credentials: true
}));
```

### 10. No Request Size Limits
```javascript
// BAD ❌
app.use(express.json()); // Unlimited size!

// GOOD ✅
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
```

