## Best Practices

### 1. Secret Generation

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD: Cryptographically secure
const crypto = require('crypto');
const secret = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex'); // 64 chars

// ✅ GOOD: Base64 encoding
const secret = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64'); // 44 chars

// ❌ BAD: Predictable
const secret = 'my-secret-key-123';

// ❌ BAD: Too short
const secret = crypto.randomBytes(8).toString('hex'); // Only 16 chars
```

### 2. Secret Length Requirements

| Secret Type | Minimum Length | Recommended |
|-------------|----------------|-------------|
| JWT Secret | 32 bytes (64 hex) | 64 bytes (128 hex) |
| Session Secret | 32 bytes | 64 bytes |
| Database Password | 16 chars | 32 chars |
| API Key | 20 chars | 40 chars |
| Encryption Key (AES-256) | 32 bytes (exact) | 32 bytes |

### 3. Secret Validation

```javascript
function validateSecret(secret, name, minLength = 32) {
  if (!secret) {
    throw new Error(`${name} is not set`);
  }

  if (secret.length < minLength) {
    throw new Error(`${name} is too short (min: ${minLength})`);
  }

  // Check for weak/default values
  const weakSecrets = ['password', 'secret', 'change-this', 'admin'];
  if (weakSecrets.some(weak => secret.toLowerCase().includes(weak))) {
    throw new Error(`${name} contains a weak/default value`);
  }

  // Check entropy
  const uniqueChars = new Set(secret).size;
  if (uniqueChars < secret.length * 0.5) {
    console.warn(`⚠️  ${name} has low entropy`);
  }
}
```

### 4. Never Do This

```javascript
// ❌ NEVER commit secrets to code
const JWT_SECRET = 'abc123def456';

// ❌ NEVER log secrets
console.log('JWT_SECRET:', process.env.JWT_SECRET);

// ❌ NEVER send secrets in responses
res.json({ secret: JWT_SECRET });

// ❌ NEVER use weak fallbacks
const secret = process.env.SECRET || 'default-secret';

// ❌ NEVER hardcode secrets in config files
module.exports = {
  jwt: { secret: 'my-secret-key' }
};
```

### 5. Always Do This

```javascript
// ✅ Load from environment
require('dotenv').config();

// ✅ Validate on startup
if (!process.env.JWT_SECRET) {
  console.error('JWT_SECRET not set');
  process.exit(1);
}

// ✅ Use centralized config
const config = {
  jwt: { secret: process.env.JWT_SECRET }
};

// ✅ Log secret status (not value!)
console.log(`JWT_SECRET: ${process.env.JWT_SECRET.length} chars`);

// ✅ Use secrets manager in production
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  // Load from AWS Secrets Manager / Vault
}
```

