## Secret Rotation

### Why Rotate Secrets?

- 🔒 Limit exposure window if compromised
- 📋 Compliance requirements (PCI DSS, SOC 2)
- 🔄 Reduce impact of insider threats
- 🛡️ Defense in depth strategy

### Rotation Schedule

| Secret Type | Rotation Frequency |
|-------------|-------------------|
| JWT Secret | Every 90 days |
| Session Secret | Every 90 days |
| Database Password | Every 60 days |
| API Keys | Every 180 days |
| SSL Certificates | Before expiry |

### Manual Rotation Process

```bash
# 1. Generate new secret
NEW_SECRET=$(node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))")

# 2. Update in secrets manager
aws secretsmanager update-secret \
  --secret-id production/JWT_SECRET \
  --secret-string "$NEW_SECRET"

# 3. Gradually roll out to servers
# Keep old secret valid during transition

# 4. After all servers updated, remove old secret

# 5. Audit access logs
aws cloudtrail lookup-events \
  --lookup-attributes AttributeKey=ResourceName,AttributeValue=production/JWT_SECRET
```

### Automated Rotation (AWS)

```javascript
// Lambda function for automatic rotation
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { SecretId, Token, Step } = event;
  const secretsmanager = new AWS.SecretsManager();

  switch (Step) {
    case 'createSecret':
      // Generate new secret
      const newSecret = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');
      await secretsmanager.putSecretValue({
        SecretId,
        ClientRequestToken: Token,
        SecretString: newSecret,
        VersionStages: ['AWSPENDING']
      }).promise();
      break;

    case 'setSecret':
      // Update application (if needed)
      break;

    case 'testSecret':
      // Verify new secret works
      break;

    case 'finishSecret':
      // Mark as current
      await secretsmanager.updateSecretVersionStage({
        SecretId,
        VersionStage: 'AWSCURRENT',
        MoveToVersionId: Token,
        RemoveFromVersionId: currentVersion
      }).promise();
      break;
  }
};
```

