## 🛡️ Security Best Practices Checklist

- [ ] **Authentication**: Implement JWT or session-based auth
- [ ] **Authorization**: Role-based access control (RBAC)
- [ ] **Input Validation**: Validate all user inputs
- [ ] **Output Encoding**: Prevent XSS attacks
- [ ] **Security Headers**: Use Helmet.js
- [ ] **HTTPS**: Force HTTPS in production
- [ ] **Rate Limiting**: Prevent abuse and DoS
- [ ] **CORS**: Configure allowed origins
- [ ] **Error Handling**: Never expose stack traces
- [ ] **Logging**: Log security events
- [ ] **Secrets Management**: Use environment variables
- [ ] **Dependencies**: Regular security audits (`npm audit`)
- [ ] **SQL Injection**: Use parameterized queries/ORMs
- [ ] **NoSQL Injection**: Sanitize MongoDB queries
- [ ] **XSS**: Sanitize user input
- [ ] **CSRF**: Implement CSRF tokens for state-changing operations
- [ ] **File Uploads**: Validate file types and sizes
- [ ] **Session Management**: Secure session configuration
- [ ] **Password Storage**: Use bcrypt/argon2 for hashing
- [ ] **API Versioning**: Version your APIs

